  "notes": [
    "HTTP status describes the current API request. Reading a FAILED refresh attempt succeeds with HTTP 200 and embeds that attempt's error.",
    "retryable is advisory for a later explicit policy-eligible operation, never automatic resubmission. A false value does not forbid a fresh user intent after changed input/policy and all gates.",
    "Null backoff means operation/state-specific policy, not zero. 429 responses carry Retry-After; daily quotas wait to the next UTC boundary.",
    "UPSTREAM_RESPONSE_REJECTED uses 3600 seconds for stable upstream 4xx, otherwise 900. No source restriction or quarantine can be bypassed after a timer.",
    "Edge/origin rejection can occur before the controlled API and need not use this JSON/code catalogue."
